@after
title: Independence won!
subtitle: ... what now?
view-if: consultation_preparation >= 6 and consultation_yes_pc > consultation_no_pc
on-arrival: {!
    if (!Q.countdowns.includes("unio_breakup")) Q.countdowns.push("unio_breakup");
    if (!Q.countdowns.includes("jxsi_formation")) Q.countdowns.push("jxsi_formation");
    Q.unio_breakup_countdown = 3;
    Q.jxsi_formation_countdown = 5;
    Q.plebiscite_election_countdown = 4;
!}

After the celebration, it is clear what the question on everyone's mind right is: what now? A non-binding consultation does not force the Generalitat into any path of action, and it is not like the current [+ cat_coalition_disp +] has made any provisions for continuing any path towards independence after this. It may be time to re-think any roadmaps towards independence...

- @post_event: Was everything just for this?

@failure
title: What a disaster...
view-if: consultation_preparation < 4
on-arrival: {!
    Q.independence_trust = Math.max(0, Q.independence_trust - 15);
    Q.independence_movement = Math.max(0, Q.independence_movement - 5);
!}
go-to: post_event

@troubled
title: We voted, but barely
view-if: consultation_preparation >= 4 and consultation_preparation < 6 and consultation_yes_pc > consultation_no_pc
call: nonbinding_consultation.after
on-arrival: {!
    Q.independence_trust = Math.max(0, Q.independence_trust - 10);
!}

Of course, and as expected, the "Yes" has won. But the organization has left much to be desired, to say the least.  There have been glaring gaps in the voting process with whole areas of the country effectively left unserved by polling spaces. This deeply unserious siutation has been heavily criticized by the pro-union parties, of course, but also by many critical voices within the independence movement. Despite the celebrations by the Generalitat as a "win for democracy", it is clear that any attempts at pursuing independence further will require a level of seriousness much beyond what has transpired today.

And even past the debate, the bigger question on everyone's mind is: what now? A non-binding consultation does not force the Generalitat into any path of action, and it is not like the current [+ cat_coalition_disp +] has made any provisions for continuing any path towards independence after this. It may be time to re-think any roadmaps towards independence...

- @post_event: Was everything just for this?

@after_no
title: This is no short of unexpected...
on-arrival: {!
    this.achieve("majoria_no_silenciosa");

    Q.independence_movement -= 30;
    Q.independence_trust -= 30;
    Q.cat_spa_relations += 25;

    if (!Q.countdowns.includes("parlament_snap_election")) Q.countdowns.push("parlament_snap_election");
    Q.parlament_snap_election_countdown = 1;

    // TODO: ramifications of what happens here besides the snap election, specially for CiU. It's virutally impossible to get to this scene though.
!}
view-if: consultation_yes_pc <= consultation_no_pc

This never-expected result has certainly caught everyone off-guard. [? if president_gender = "m": President ?][? if president_gender = "f": Presidenta ?][+ president +] is under heavy pressure now, with voices from all the Parlament's spectrum, including their own party, to hold elections. As for us, the future is as blurry as it can get. This may very well be the end of the independence movement for this generation.

- @post_event: Was everything just for this?
